{
 "about": "Field classes of the admin_inventory domain (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.3, lint L-WATCH; WP-D admin_inventory). 'fields' classifies, for this domain's types (house_sim/data/types/admin_inventory.json), every property of the type data and every field this domain's verbs and systems write on them, explicitly -- names the kernel's watch_fields.json already classifies are restated with the kernel's class, and a few it misfits for these types are overridden: identity = what a thing is, its printed text and ratings (a document's text, title, date and sensitivity; an envelope's to_text / from_text; a tag's text; a printer's power_w and duty cycle, a pen's dry-out time, a scale's resolution and a dispenser's fill line are ratings, not process or content); setting = a configuration the robot sets (fold, staple position, tape seal, outgoing flag, roll orientation, a cartridge's protective tape and clip, zipped); condition = damage in its worse direction (true is worse unless 'worse' says false, up or change: pages out of order, a bent staple, an unscannable label, punched holes, creases, mildew); content = what it holds (tissues, a counted pack's units, a paper stack's sheets, a napkin stack's napkins, a pen's ink, a printer's files; the chad in a punch's tray and the strips in a shredder bin are mess loads the mess balance judges, guard mess); process = transient state (the print queue, a shredder's thermal cutout, a pencil's sharpness); bookkeeping = records, counters and mirrors of other things' placements (a bag's load_kg / fill_l / tagged, a paper tray's sheets_loaded / sizes_loaded, a napkin holder's napkins / dispensable / fill, slots, a parcel's label verdicts, the refuse flag waste and hazard tags: the things themselves, their placements and the mess balance are judged). 'types': names that mean something else on a type. 'water_sensitive': paper and cardboard goods, paper documents and mail, and the domain's electronics (house.wet).",
